--TEST--
`self`, `static` and `parent` written where a value is expected are each `E0321`, never a panic — all three name a class, and `rule:classes/no-free-functions-or-constants` leaves no class handle for one to evaluate to
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Base {
    public static function n(): int {
        return 1;
    }
}

final class C extends Base {
    // Each of the three names a class. There is no class-object value in
    // Novis for one to evaluate to — `rule:classes/no-free-functions-or-constants` puts every reflective question
    // on `Core\Reflect` — so a bare occurrence is refused where it is
    // written rather than reaching `nvs-ir`'s dispatch.
    public static function a(): mixed {
        return self;
    }

    public static function b(): mixed {
        return static;
    }

    public static function c(): mixed {
        return parent;
    }

    // The control: the same three words on the left of a `::` are class
    // sides, not values, so none of them is reported and the expectation
    // below carries exactly three diagnostics.
    public static function d(): int {
        return self::n() + parent::n() + static::n();
    }
}
echo "unreached\n";
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0321]: `self` names a class, and a class is not a value
   --> %s:14:16
   |
14 |         return self;
   |                ^^^^ used where a value is expected
   = help: write `self::` and the member wanted — a method call, a constant or a static property. There is no class handle to pass around: `rule:classes/no-free-functions-or-constants` puts every reflective question on `Core\Reflect` instead

error[E0321]: `static` names a class, and a class is not a value
   --> %s:18:16
   |
18 |         return static;
   |                ^^^^^^ used where a value is expected
   = help: write `static::` and the member wanted — a method call, a constant or a static property. There is no class handle to pass around: `rule:classes/no-free-functions-or-constants` puts every reflective question on `Core\Reflect` instead

error[E0321]: `parent` names a class, and a class is not a value
   --> %s:22:16
   |
22 |         return parent;
   |                ^^^^^^ used where a value is expected
   = help: write `parent::` and the member wanted — a method call, a constant or a static property. There is no class handle to pass around: `rule:classes/no-free-functions-or-constants` puts every reflective question on `Core\Reflect` instead

